**Results** (`results/histogram_T5Wg.yaml`):

| S_T^γ bin | Predicted yield (35.9 fb⁻¹) |
|---|---|
| 600–800 GeV | 0.086 |
| 800–1000 GeV | 0.420 |
| 1000–1300 GeV | 1.174 |
| >1300 GeV | 3.193 |

**Total signal yield: ~4.87 events** at 35.9 fb⁻¹ for T5Wg_1750_1700.

The distribution is strongly peaked in the high-S_T^γ tail (>1300 GeV bin), consistent with hard photons from the χ̃⁰₁→γG̃ decay and large MET from the near-massless gravitino LSP carrying away most of the wino momentum.

**Key fix that unblocked Delphes:** The HepMC3 AsciiV3 format requires `E N 1 M` (nVertices=1 in the header) with an explicit `V -1 0 []` line, then all final-state particles written as `P id 0 pid ...` (OutVertexCode=0). With OutVertexCode=0, Delphes creates an implicit "vertex 0" on the first particle line, decrementing `fVertexCounter` from 0 to -1, which satisfies `EventReady()`. Previous attempts used OutVertexCode=-1, which recycled the existing vertex -1 without decrementing — so `EventReady()` never fired.
